(footprint "Analog_LGA-25_6.25x6.25mm_Layout5x5_P1.27mm"
  (descr "LTM4622 LGA-25, 6.25 x 6.25 mm, 1.27 mm pitch. Hand drawn.

   AXIS CONVENTION, and read this before editing: from Rev G's PIN
   CONFIGURATION top view, letters run A..E LEFT TO RIGHT and numbers run
   1..5 BOTTOM TO TOP. KiCad's +Y is down the page, so row 5 sits at the
   most negative y and A1 is the BOTTOM-LEFT land.

   The drawing does not survive text extraction from the PDF, so the check
   that settles it is PIN FUNCTIONS, which does: COMP2 (A5), SYNC/MODE (C5)
   and COMP1 (E5) are the three named balls in row 5, and the drawing prints
   that row left to right as COMP2 / GND / SYNC-MODE / GND / COMP1. If the
   letters ran the other way that row would start with COMP1; if the numbers
   ran the other way the top row would be row 1, which is VOUT2 / VOUT2 /
   GND / VOUT1 / VOUT1.

   This footprint had the two axes transposed, which put 24 of 25 lands on
   the wrong ball -- +2V5 and +5V onto VOUT2, the 1.0 V core rail with a
   1.20 V absolute maximum. Only C3 at the centre was invariant.")
  (version 20240108) (generator "lyrebird") (layer "F.Cu")
  (descr "Analog Devices LGA-25, 6.25x6.25x1.82mm, 1.27mm pitch, 0.635mm lands. Geometry from the LTM4622 datasheet suggested PCB layout.")
  (tags "LGA 25 uModule 1.27mm")
  (attr smd)
  (property "Reference" "U" (at 0 -4.2 0) (layer "F.SilkS")
    (effects (font (size 1 1) (thickness 0.15))))
  (property "Value" "LTM4622" (at 0 4.2 0) (layer "F.Fab")
    (effects (font (size 1 1) (thickness 0.15))))
  (fp_rect (start -3.375 -3.375) (end 3.375 3.375) (stroke (width 0.05) (type solid)) (fill none) (layer "F.CrtYd"))
